---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Scholarship"
	description="Gavin Keulks — chapters and essays on the Amises, postmodernism and contemporary fiction, visual culture, and Aldous Huxley."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Scholarship</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">
				Work for both general and specialized audiences, organized by theme.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="work">
			<h2>Contemporary Fiction (Amises, Rushdie, Winterson)</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Staging Amis: Autobiography and Autofiction.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>The Cambridge&nbsp;Companion to Martin&nbsp;Amis</em>. Cambridge
					University Press, 2026. 211&ndash;27. Also the Introduction, 1&ndash;10.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;&lsquo;No less than we deserve&rsquo;: the Traditional Roots
						of the Amises&rsquo; Contemporary Satires.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Critical Engagements</em> 3.2 (satire issue, Winter 2010): 35&ndash;51.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;&lsquo;Preferring the composite darkness&rsquo;: Trauma Theory
						and Narration in <em>The Ground Beneath Her Feet</em> and{' '}
						<em>Shalimar the Clown</em>.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Rushdie the Novelist: from Grimus to The Enchantress of Florence</em
					>. Ed. Meenakshi Bharat. Pencraft International, 2008. 247&ndash;63.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;New York, Los Angeles, and Other Toxicities: Revisiting
						Postmodernism in Rushdie&rsquo;s <em>Fury</em> and{' '}
						<em>Shalimar the Clown</em>.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>The Mourning After: Attending the Wake of Postmodernism</em>. Eds.
					Neil Brooks and Josh Toth. Rodopi, 2007. 143&ndash;68.{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Mourning_After/S2t2m20XVHkC?hl=en&amp;gbpv=1&amp;pg=PA143" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Google&nbsp;Books preview</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Winterson&rsquo;s Recent Work: Navigating Realism and
						Postmodernism.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Jeanette Winterson: A Contemporary Critical Guide</em>. Ed. Sonya
					Andermahr. Continuum, 2007. 146&ndash;62.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;W(h)ither Postmodernism: Late Amis.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Martin Amis: Postmodernism and Beyond</em>. Palgrave Macmillan,
					2006. 158&ndash;79. Also the Introduction, 1&ndash;8.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="work">
			<h2>Visual Culture and Advertising</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Visualizing the Virtual: Alejandro
						G.&nbsp;I&ntilde;&aacute;rritu&rsquo;s{' '}
						<em>CARNE y ARENA</em>, A Case Study.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Advertising and Society</em>. Cognella. Accepted for publication.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;The Artful Marketing of Irish Culture: Dublin&rsquo;s Icon
						Walk.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Advertising and Society</em>. Cognella. Accepted for publication.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;YOLO&rsquo;ing your Book Launch, or (ahem) Multi-channel
						Cross-promotion for the Digital Age.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Invited blogpost. <em>Fifteen Eighty Four</em>, Academic Perspectives
					from Cambridge University&nbsp;Press. 21&nbsp;July&nbsp;2026.{' '}
					<a
						href="https://cambridgeblog.org/2026/07/yoloing-your-book-launch-or-ahemmulti-channel-cross-promotionfor-the-digital-age/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>cambridgeblog.org</a
					>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="work">
			<h2>General Reference</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Aldous Huxley: A Centenary Bibliography
						(1978&ndash;1995).&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>Journal of Modern Literature</em> 20.2 (Winter 1996): 223&ndash;38.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>Nine entries for the{' '}
						<em>Oxford Encyclopedia of British Literature</em>.</span
					>{' '}
					Eds. David Scott Kastan et&nbsp;al. Oxford University Press, 2005. On
					Elizabeth Bowen, Arthur Conan Doyle, Graham Greene, Aldous Huxley, Kazuo
					Ishiguro, David Lodge, Edna O&rsquo;Brien, Salman Rushdie, and Jeanette
					Winterson.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Kingsley Amis&rdquo; and &ldquo;Martin Amis.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>The Blackwell Encyclopedia of Twentieth-Century Fiction</em>. Eds.
					Brian Shaffer et&nbsp;al. Blackwell, 2011.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Kingsley Amis.&rdquo;</span>{' '}
					<em>The Literary Encyclopedia</em>. Eds. Robert Clark, Emory Elliott, and
					Janet Todd. The Literary Dictionary Company, 2005.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<p class="cv-line">
			A complete list of publications and papers appears in my{' '}
			<a href="/documents/gavin-keulks-cv.pdf">curriculum vitae (PDF)</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.page-intro {
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 0.6vw, 1.3rem);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.work {
		padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.work h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
	}

	.cite-list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.cite-list li {
		padding-block: 0.7rem;
		padding-left: 1.4rem;
		text-indent: -1.4rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.cite-list li + li {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.cite-title {
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}

	.cv-line {
		margin: 0;
		text-align: center;
		padding-block: 1.35rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.cv-line a {
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}
</style>
